# Round 19 (writer 10): settled; was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.16. GD-24, C4-11: L §5.16's table "over a key list or a stepped range it is refused (LOAD-DOMAIN)"; L §8.3
# `discrete over a key list or a stepped range`. The old comment:
# L §5.16 The closed list: `discrete(w for k in IDX)`, "its values are the keys of IDX, in index order". A binding over
# a key list (or a stepped range) is no index: what such a draw's values are, and their order, the spec doesn't state,
# so refcore keeps REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.16 here (the one site left, UNSPECIFIED.md).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input w: num
def g: dist = discrete(w for k in [a, b])

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = 1

ask q: quantile(g, 50 %)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN discrete over a key list or a stepped range (m.tally:9)
